<article class="env-definition" id="0EJ3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EJ3">Definition <span data-tag="0EJ3">52.19.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EHC" data-tag="0EHC">52.16.1</a> let $(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ be an object of $\textit{Coh}(U, I\mathcal{O}_ U)$. Let $a, b$ be integers. Let $\delta ^ Y_ Z$ be as in (<a href="/tag/0EIX" data-tag="0EIX">52.18.0.1</a>). We say <em>$(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ satisfies the $(a, b)$-inequalities</em> if for $y \in U \cap Y$ and a prime $\mathfrak p \subset \mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge $ with $\mathfrak p \not\in V(I\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge )$ </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
if $V(\mathfrak p) \cap V(I\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge ) \not= \{ \mathfrak m_ y^\wedge \} $, then 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \text{depth}((\mathcal{F}^\wedge _ y)_\mathfrak p) + \delta ^ Y_ Z(y) \geq a \quad \text{or}\quad \text{depth}((\mathcal{F}^\wedge _ y)_\mathfrak p) + \dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge /\mathfrak p) + \delta ^ Y_ Z(y) > b  \]
</div>
</li><li><p>
if $V(\mathfrak p) \cap V(I\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge ) = \{ \mathfrak m_ y^\wedge \} $, then 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \text{depth}((\mathcal{F}^\wedge _ y)_\mathfrak p) + \delta ^ Y_ Z(y) > a  \]
</div>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> We say <em>$(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ satisfies the strict $(a, b)$-inequalities</em> if for $y \in U \cap Y$ and a prime $\mathfrak p \subset \mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge $ with $\mathfrak p \not\in V(I\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge )$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{depth}((\mathcal{F}^\wedge _ y)_\mathfrak p) + \delta ^ Y_ Z(y) > a \quad \text{or}\quad \text{depth}((\mathcal{F}^\wedge _ y)_\mathfrak p) + \dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge /\mathfrak p) + \delta ^ Y_ Z(y) > b  \]
</div>
</article>